@startuml
title UC-06 - internal-k8s happy path
autonumber
actor Developer
control DeploymentService as Service
control PlanningService as Planner
control ImplicitResourceEnricher as Enricher
control ResourceProvisioningService as Provisioner
boundary ExistingClusterAdapter as ExistingCluster
boundary TerraformExecutor as ResourceTF
control OutputBindingResolver as Resolver
control WorkloadRenderer as Renderer
boundary WorkloadDeployer as WorkloadK8s
boundary PublicRouteManager as Routes
control ConnectionCredentialResolver as Credentials
database DeploymentRepository as Repo

Developer -> Service: DeployWorkload(Score, app, env)
Service -> Repo: Create PLANNING [MS-01]
Service -> Planner: Plan(request) [MS-02..MS-04]
Planner -> Enricher: Enrich(profile=internal-k8s) [MS-05]
Enricher --> Planner: implicit cluster from pinned Environment Connection + env namespace
Planner -> Planner: Bind cluster with system existing-cluster; match other Definitions [BR-20..BR-21]
note right of Planner: Mismatch fails planning before execution; no default fallback
Planner --> Service: Humanitec-shaped Delta + graph:\nworkload -> namespace -> existing cluster\nworkload -> postgres in-cluster -> namespace -> existing cluster [MS-03..MS-08]
group Required score-k8s preflight
  Service -> Renderer: ValidateSelection(pinned bundle/binary) before side effects
  Renderer --> Service: available
end
Service -> Repo: Admit Environment owner/fence under pinned versions
Service -> Provisioner: Provision(resource batches, owner/fence) [MS-09]
Provisioner -> Repo: Admit reserved system Definition (idempotent; collision fails)
Provisioner -> ExistingCluster: Resolve/check pinned cluster reference
ExistingCluster -> Credentials: Resolve scoped selected Connection
Credentials --> ExistingCluster: private invocation credential
ExistingCluster --> Provisioner: opaque Kubernetes target (org + connection)
Provisioner -> ResourceTF: Provision(namespace, target)
ResourceTF --> Provisioner: namespace output
Provisioner -> ResourceTF: Provision(PostgreSQL module, same Kubernetes target/state backend)
ResourceTF --> Provisioner: postgres outputs
Provisioner -> ResourceTF: Provision(Redis module, same target/state backend)
ResourceTF --> Provisioner: Redis outputs
Provisioner --> Service: outputs + internal target
Service -> Resolver: ResolveWorkloadBindings(postgres + Redis outputs) [MS-10]
Resolver --> Service: Resolved target workload
Service -> Renderer: Render(normalized workload, output-only bindings, pinned bundle) [MS-11]
Renderer -> Renderer: score-k8s init (no defaults), generate, controlled patches
Renderer -> Renderer: Validate protected identity/namespace/Secret refs
Renderer --> Service: validated Service/Deployment + Secret/Agent auxiliary objects
Service -> WorkloadK8s: Apply(internal target, manifests)
WorkloadK8s -> Credentials: Resolve scoped credential for this invocation
Credentials --> WorkloadK8s: private kubeconfig + cleanup
Service -> WorkloadK8s: WaitReady(target workload)
WorkloadK8s --> Service: Ready
opt Direct UC-06 (pending batch defers until all affected workloads ready)
  Service -> Routes: Reconcile Environment Ingress from Candidate Set
  Routes --> Service: Ingress applied or Fleet bundle observed
end
note over Provisioner, Repo
Fresh/reused resource targets retain Connection identity.
Workload TargetRef persists identity, never secret/temp path.
end note
Service -> Repo: Commit set/resources/workloads/SUCCEEDED [MS-12]
Service --> Developer: DeploymentResult [MS-13]
note over Developer, Service
Acceptance verification repeats this operation for
backend, worker and frontend declared through existing forms.
Then browser submits job and verifies PostgreSQL + Redis use.
end note

@enduml
